## Sound effects and music (sound v2: research/sound-v2.md is the cue spec, the sonic brief and
## the mix; research/sound-v2-runtime-audit.md the runtime design). Every sound is generated by
## tools/audio.sh (original, no licensed assets; assets_src/audio/LICENSES.csv lists each file).
##
## Buses, created in code (sound-v2 §6.1): 3 effects always on, 2 only while needed.
##   Master    a hard limiter at -1 dB
##   Music     a compressor keyed from Critical (ducks under threats); one low-pass, on only
##             while a snapshot closes it (menu, low HP, death). Chorus and reverb are baked.
##   SFX       combat chatter; a compressor keyed from Critical pulls it under threats
##     Glitch  -> SFX: a LOFI distortion, on only while Copy-Paste's copies of your spells play
##   Critical  -> Master, dry: hurt, telegraphs, boss moments
##   Sting     -> Master: stingers (the music ducks under them by a tween)
##   UI        menus
##   Ambience  the area bed and its spots
## Sound off mutes SFX, Critical, UI and Ambience; Music off mutes Music and Sting.
##
## One-shots: every call site asks for a cue id (and where it happened); the request waits for
## the end of the frame. flush() then merges repeats of a cue, sorts by priority, starts at most
## a budget of new voices, and steals only from voices that do not outrank the new cue. All
## per-cue behaviour is the CUES table below: call sites pass context, never a volume.
##
## Music: title | shop | cellar | grove | foundry | kernel | mini | boss. Area tracks are stems in an
## AudioStreamSynchronized (base; drums while fighting; the lead at intensity 2). Every layer
## switch lands on the next bar of the music's own sample clock.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the cue table

## One row per cue id: the file is res://assets/audio/sfx_<id>.wav, with variants _2, _3, ...
## (picked at random, never the same twice in a row). A field missing from a row comes from
## its group (GROUPS), then its class (CLASSES), then CUE_DEFAULT; an id with no row plays with
## the defaults, and an id with no file plays nothing (or its `fallback` cue's files).
## Fields (sound-v2 §6.2):
##   class         "crit" (Critical) | "cmb" (SFX) | "ui" (UI) | "det" (SFX, lowest)
##   prio          0-100: the budget keeps the highest; a steal takes the weakest voice that
##                 does not outrank the new cue (lowest prio, then quietest, then least left)
##   group, cap    at most `cap` voices of the group at once (the group defaults to the id)
##   gap           seconds: a repeat sooner than this is dropped
##   gain_db       added to the file's level (0: the hierarchy lives in the files, §4.1)
##   jitter_cents  random pitch +/- cents;  vol_db  random gain +/- dB
##   pan           true: panned by where it happened; false: centred
##   walk          "" | "chain" (repeats within walk_win climb the key's pentatonic, held to
##                 walk_reset, up to walk_max) | "slot" (wand slot) | "depth" (trigger depth)
##                 | "count" (pylon hits 1-4)
##   semis         a fixed pitch offset;  bus  a bus other than the class's
##   fallback      another cue whose files play while this one has none (interim)
##   fam, lufs     the loudness family of the file (§4.1: W C C+ E A M U U+) and, where the
##                 spec gives one, the cue's own target in LUFS-M (the tests check the files)
##   hook_pending  a cue with no call site yet (the tests allow it)
